{{was wotd|2007|June|14}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[lambast]] ''(UK)''

===Etymology===
First attested in 1637.  Probably {{compound|lam|gloss1=beat|baste|gloss2=beat}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/læmˈbæst/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/læmˈbæst/|/læmˈbeɪst/}}
* {{audio|en-us-lambaste.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|æst}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|lambast|ing}}

# To [[scold]], [[reprimand]] or criticize harshly.
#: ''The sergeant '''lambasted''' the new recruits daily.''
#: ''Her first novel was well and truly '''lambasted''' by the critics.''
# {{dated}} To give a [[thrash]]ing to; to [[beat]] severely.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to give a thrashing to}} [[beat]], [[hit]], [[thrash]]
* {{sense|to scold or verbally reprimand}} [[berate]], [[scold]], [[tell off]]

